<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Description de l'Égypte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1809–1829</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Description de l'Égypte is a large illustrated survey of ancient and modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and its natural history, compiled by the scholars who accompanied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s expedition of 1798–1801. Published by the French government in many volumes between 1809 and 1829, its plates of temples, monuments, plants and daily life greatly stimulated European interest in Egypt and helped lay the foundations of Egyptology.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/description-de-legypte.jpg" alt="Description de l'Égypte" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Description_de_l%C2%B4Egypte_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
